        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear Colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your 85-year-old male patient, admitted on 28th May 1982 due to an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, physical examination revealed decreased air entry bilaterally with expiratory wheeze. Chest X-ray confirmed pulmonary hyperinflation without evidence of pneumonia or pneumothorax. Arterial blood gas analysis demonstrated hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia. Blood tests showed mild inflammatory markers. Pulse oximetry was monitored continuously throughout the stay. The patient was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and intravenous fluids. He responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. Patient education regarding inhaler technique and exacerbation management was provided prior to discharge. Please ensure follow-up within two weeks. Do not hesitate to contact me for further information. Yours sincerely, Dr. [Treating Physician]</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
